From 567e3d559c54220604796f82e8bac38a2f3760c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BHARATH CHANDRA VADDARAM <bharath.vbcr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:00:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Stop reporting an overwritten error on a call whose
 results are all blanked

`_, _ = w.Write(nil)` blanks the error explicitly, which docs/RULES.md accepts as the discard
escape, but only assignments that kept a companion value were recorded as blanked. For the
all-blank form go/ssa still emits the error Extract, lowering bound it to a slot nothing reads, and
the next trip round a loop rebound it and reported ERR003. The all-blank calls are now recorded by
exact Lparen, in a set no same-line fallback can claim for a neighbouring call, and lowered as a
blanked tuple with no error slot.

Six fixture markers pinned the false positive and move in this commit, each with a ft-c7dd
comment: advfv3b3c/a.go:68, advfvrange3b3c/r.go:30, adv2fvstore/s.go:108, 120 and 132 and
adv2fvstore2/s.go:31. A real overwrite in a loop (`_, err = w.Write(nil)` with err unread) is still
reported, and a fixture pins it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
